# 2D sheared granular flow with EVERY dimensionless group held fixed except
# kappa = E/P.  The corrected pressure lever.
#
# The original pressure lever (Result 6) was abandoned as physically
# impossible: holding I fixed forces gdot ~ sqrt(P), and the resulting shear
# heating overwhelmed the thermostat (at Pconf=50 the measured Theta was
# 6x its setpoint and non-monotonic). The stated conclusion was that escaping
# it needs a stronger bath, but since n depends on t_damp that would change
# the physics.
#
# That conflated a DIMENSIONAL parameter with a DIMENSIONLESS group. n depends
# on Pi_damp = t_damp*sqrt(P/rho)/d, not on t_damp in absolute time units.
# t_damp = 0.5 was hardcoded everywhere, so raising P silently RAISED Pi_damp
# -- a bath that damps slowly compared to grain dynamics -- precisely where
# shear heating was strongest. Holding Pi_damp fixed instead means t_damp must
# FALL as 1/sqrt(P), giving a stiffer bath at higher pressure. That is not a
# change of physics; it is what keeping the physics fixed actually requires.
#
# Four quantities therefore scale together with pressure:
#   gdot   ~ sqrt(P)     holds I = gdot*d*sqrt(rho/P) fixed
#   t_damp ~ 1/sqrt(P)   holds Pi_damp fixed
#   Tgran  ~ P           holds the DIMENSIONLESS Theta = rho<dv^2>/P window
#                        fixed. Note the code's `Theta` output is the raw
#                        LAMMPS temperature c_tbias, not Theta itself; within
#                        one pressure the constant drops out of the log-slope,
#                        but across pressures the same Tgran grid would sample
#                        a different dimensionless window, and mu(Theta) has
#                        measurable curvature.
#   dt     ~ 1/sqrt(P)   conservative for stability, and since gdot ~ sqrt(P)
#                        the product dt*gdot is invariant, so a fixed step
#                        count covers a fixed STRAIN.
#
# With those, a pressure scan moves kappa alone and nothing else.
#
# Usage:
#   lmp -in in.granular_2d_piscan -var datafile data.q -var mu_g 0.3 \
#       -var Pconf 50.0 -var gdot 2.236e-3 -var tdamp 0.2236 \
#       -var Tgran 0.10 -var dt 4.472e-4 -var seed 1 -var label p50

variable datafile index data.granular
variable mu_g     index 0.3
variable gdot     index 1.0e-3
variable Tgran    index 0.003
variable Pconf    index 10.0
variable tdamp    index 0.5
variable dt       index 0.001
variable seed     index 12345
variable label    index piscan
variable nequil   index 40000
variable nmeas    index 80000

units           lj
dimension       2
atom_style      sphere
boundary        p p p
newton          off

read_data       ${datafile}

pair_style      granular
pair_coeff      * * hertz/material 1.0e5 0.3 0.5 tangential mindlin NULL 1.0 ${mu_g} damping tsuji

neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
comm_modify     vel yes

fix             integrate all nve/sphere
fix             damp all viscous 1.0
timestep        ${dt}
thermo          1000
thermo_style    custom step ke
run             3000
unfix           damp
unfix           integrate
velocity        all set 0.0 0.0 0.0
reset_timestep  0

change_box      all triclinic
fix             shear all deform 1 xy erate ${gdot} remap v units box
compute         tbias all temp/deform
fix             therm all langevin ${Tgran} ${Tgran} ${tdamp} ${seed} zero yes
fix_modify      therm temp tbias
compute         press all pressure tbias
fix             baro all nph/sphere y ${Pconf} ${Pconf} 1.0 ptemp ${Tgran}
fix_modify      baro press press

compute         cont all contact/atom
compute         Zbulk all reduce ave c_cont

variable        P      equal (c_press[1]+c_press[2])/2.0
variable        tau    equal c_press[4]
variable        muI    equal abs(v_tau)/v_P
variable        Theta  equal c_tbias
variable        rmean  equal 0.5
variable        Iiner  equal ${gdot}*2.0*v_rmean/sqrt(v_P)
variable        Zc     equal c_Zbulk
# dimensionless granular temperature, reported explicitly so the scanned
# window can be verified as matched across pressures rather than assumed
variable        Thnd   equal c_tbias/v_P

thermo_style    custom step v_P v_tau v_muI c_tbias v_Theta v_Iiner v_Zc v_Thnd
thermo          2000
log             log.${label} append

run             ${nequil}
print           "=== BEGIN MEASUREMENT WINDOW ${label} ==="
run             ${nmeas}
print           "DONE label=${label} mu_g=${mu_g} Pconf=${Pconf} tdamp=${tdamp} Tgran=${Tgran} Z=$(c_Zbulk)"
